# ── MARK LIII — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# (Git only treats # as a comment at the START of a line — so each comment sits
#  on its own line above its pattern. A comment after a pattern breaks the pattern.)
# your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials
config/api_keys.json
# the dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
config/certs/
# a LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody your WhatsApp account
config/whatsapp_web/
# Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/token*.json
# Google OAuth client secrets
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# Locked keys and every settings file JARVIS writes for you (all created at run time)
config/*.json
config/*.locked
config/*.tmp
config/lights.json

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/*.json
memory/*.db
memory/chat_history/
memory/journal/
# JARVIS's own log + tool history (2.6) — personal
memory/logs/

# ── Local-only folders ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
backups/
installer/
platform-tools/
models/

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
